libapache2-mod-coraza (0.22.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New upstream release 0.22.0.
  * Require libcoraza >= 1.8.0; support for 1.7 is dropped. The module needs
    coraza_is_response_body_accessible(), new in 1.8, to know whether a
    response body will be inspected; it refuses to load against an older
    shared library.
  * The request body read for inspection is now handed on to the application
    (replayed by the CORAZA_IN filter, spooled to disk above
    CorazaRequestBodyInMemoryLimit); handlers no longer see an empty body.
  * Response headers are no longer held back when the body will not be
    inspected: phase 4 is finalised before the headers go out, so streaming
    responses reach the client at once while phase-4 rules on non-body
    variables still deny cleanly, SSE included.
  * A deny decided in the output filter now reaches the configured
    ErrorDocument instead of httpd's recursive-error page.
  * Delayed response buckets are set aside: a proxied response under the
    header delay could previously be released corrupted.
  * The transaction is reused across internal redirects (ErrorDocument,
    FallbackResource) instead of re-inspecting; a WAF cache hit now compares
    the rule content, not just hash and count; every engine result is checked
    and fails closed; SecRemoteRules and a ruleless "Coraza On" are rejected
    at httpd -t; the protocol version is reported as it arrived.
  * Performance: request and response headers are submitted in bulk, the
    body is read in 64 KiB chunks, and it is not submitted to the engine when
    body access is off.

 -- Pierre Pomes <pierre.pomes@gmail.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

libapache2-mod-coraza (0.21.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New upstream release 0.21.0.
  * Require libcoraza >= 1.7.0; support for older libcoraza is dropped. The
    module gates on coraza_version_num() at startup and refuses to load
    against an older shared library, and always uses the tri-state
    coraza_result_t return contract.

 -- Pierre Pomes <pierre.pomes@gmail.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

libapache2-mod-coraza (0.20.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New upstream release 0.20.0. Version aligned with the coraza-nginx
    connector so the Coraza connectors share one version line.
  * Security: fail closed when request-body, response-body, or body-phase
    submission to Coraza fails, and validate the transaction handle in
    create_ctx; guard size_t-to-int narrowing at the cgo boundary.
  * Correctness: report REQUEST_PROTOCOL in slash-delimited form; sanitize
    control bytes in the synthesized Location header.
  * Streaming / memory: stream Server-Sent Events responses instead of
    buffering them, and cap delayed response-body buffering to bound worker
    memory.
  * Keep libcoraza loaded for the process lifetime (the Go runtime cannot be
    unloaded).

 -- Pierre Pomes <pierre.pomes@gmail.com>  Mon, 25 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

